#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_cache_dir.rst:15
msgid "``build_cache_dir``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_cache_dir.rst:17
msgid "Type: ``DirPath`` | Multiple: ``No`` | Default: None (Disabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_cache_dir.rst:19
msgid ""
":ref:`piocore` uses this folder to store derived files from a build system "
"(objects, firmwares, ELFs). These files are shared between all build "
"environments. To speed up a build process, you can use the same cache folder "
"between different projects if they depend on the same development platform "
"and framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_cache_dir.rst:25
msgid ""
"This option can also be configured by the global environment variable :"
"envvar:`PLATFORMIO_BUILD_CACHE_DIR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projectconf/sections/platformio/options/directory/build_cache_dir.rst:28
msgid ""
"The example of :ref:`projectconf` below instructs PlatformIO Build System to "
"check :ref:`projectconf_pio_build_cache_dir` for already compiled objects "
"for :ref:`framework_stm32cube` and project source files. The cached object "
"will not be used if the original source file was modified or build "
"environment has a different configuration (new build flags, etc):"
msgstr ""
